Q("C", 2, [P("Given below are components that facilitate transfer of molecules across phospholipid bilayers (Column X) and the properties of these components (Column Y)."),
  MATCH([["A. ATP powered pumps", "I. Movement of molecules against concentration gradient coupled to another molecule moving down the concentration gradient"],
         ["B. Uniporter", "II. Free diffusion of hydrophilic molecules"],
         ["C. Channels", "III. Movement of molecules against a concentration gradient and/or electric potential"],
         ["D. Symporter", "IV. Transport of hydrophilic molecules down their concentration gradients"]],
        ("Column X: Membrane component", "Column Y: Activity")),
  P("Choose the option that correctly matches the components with their properties.")],
  ["A (IV) B (II) C (I) D (III)", "A (II) B (III) C (IV) D (I)", "A (III) B (IV) C (I) D (II)", "A (III) B (IV) C (II) D (I)"],
  E("ATP-powered pumps (P-, V-, F-type, ABC) move solutes uphill against concentration or electrochemical gradients (III). Uniporters carry one solute by facilitated diffusion down its gradient (IV). Channels form aqueous pores that allow fast, free diffusion of specific ions or water (II). Symporters couple uphill transport of one solute to downhill movement of a co-transported ion such as Na⁺ (I).",
    {"1": "Pumps are not passive carriers.", "2": "Pumps do not allow free diffusion, and uniporters do not pump uphill.", "3": "Channels do not perform coupled transport, and symporters are not free-diffusion pores."})),
