Q("C", 1, [P("If a 0.1 M solution of glucose 1-phosphate is incubated with a catalytic amount of phosphoglucomutase, the glucose 1-phosphate is transformed to glucose 6-phosphate. At equilibrium, the concentrations of the reaction components are:"), P("Glucose 1-phosphate (4.5 × 10<sup>−3</sup> M) ⇌ Glucose 6-phosphate (9.6 × 10<sup>−2</sup> M)"), P("What would be the calculated values for K′<sub>eq</sub> and ΔG°′ for this reaction at 25°C?")],
  ["(0.0045 to 0.096) and (−0.7 to −0.8) kJ/mol", "(21 to 22) and (−7.5 to −7.7) kJ/mol", "(0.1 to 0.2) and (−17.6 to −17.7) kJ/mol", "(21 to 22) and (−27.7 to −27.8) kJ/mol"],
  E("K′<sub>eq</sub> = [G6P]/[G1P] = 0.096/0.0045 = 21.3. ΔG°′ = −RT ln K′<sub>eq</sub> = −(8.315 × 10⁻³ kJ mol⁻¹ K⁻¹)(298 K)(ln 21.3 = 3.06) = −7.6 kJ/mol. This is Lehninger's worked example; the textbook value is −7.3 kJ/mol.",
    {"1": "Uses the concentrations themselves rather than their ratio.", "3": "Inverts or misuses the ratio.", "4": "The right K′<sub>eq</sub> but a ΔG°′ off by a factor of about 3.6 (e.g. using log₁₀ wrongly, or wrong units)."})),
