Q("C", 14, [P("A purified 150 kDa protein species from gel filtration column was run on a 2-dimensional SDS-PAGE as shown below:"),
  IMG("C27", "Two-dimensional gel: first dimension SDS-PAGE (non-reducing, left to right), second dimension SDS-PAGE with DTT (top to bottom); two spots lie one above the other at the same first-dimension position"),
  P("What is the likely form of the 150 kDa protein species from this observation?")],
  ["There are at least two proteins that are linked through non-covalent interactions.", "There are at least two proteins in the complex that are linked through covalent bonds.", "There are two proteins in the mixture without forming a complex.", "There is only one protein that has a disulfide bond."],
  E("This is a diagonal (non-reducing → reducing) gel. In the first dimension, without DTT, SDS already disrupts non-covalent interactions, so the 150 kDa species runs as a single disulfide-intact unit. Reduction before the second dimension breaks S–S bonds. Two spots that share one first-dimension position but separate in the second show that the 150 kDa species consists of at least two different polypeptides joined by interchain disulfide bonds (as in IgG heavy and light chains).",
    {"1": "Non-covalent partners would already separate in the first (SDS) dimension.", "3": "Unlinked proteins would separate in the first dimension and lie on the diagonal."},
    ["NTA's final key accepts option 2 <b>or</b> option 4: either answer earns full marks. Option 2 is the interpretation that fits two spots in one first-dimension column. A single chain with an intrachain disulfide would give one spot shifted slightly off the diagonal."]),
  accept=["2", "4"]),
