Q("C", 14, [P("A student used four 20-mer oligos to amplify DNA (using a regular Taq DNA polymerase) from a wild type (WT), a homozygous mutant having a deletion of the gene (del), and from the heterozygous mutant (het), as shown in the figure below."),
  IMG("C33a", "Map: primer FW and, 500 bp downstream of it, primer FD point right towards a 15 kb deletion; primer D points left from 500 bp inside the deleted region; primer R points left 300 bp beyond the right end of the deletion"),
  P("Agarose gel electrophoresis profiles, using all four primers simultaneously, on each template are shown below. Which one of the options given below represents the correct profile?"),
  IMG("C33b", "Four gel options with lanes WT, het, del and markers 1000, 750 and 500 bp. 1: WT 1000+500, het 1000+750+500, del 750+500. 2: WT 1000+500, het 1000+750+500, del 750 only. 3: WT two bands near 1000 plus 500, het same plus 750, del about 1000 and 750. 4: WT 1000+500, het 1000+750+two bands near 500, del 750+500")],
  ["Profile 1", "Profile 2", "Profile 3", "Profile 4"],
  E("Taq cannot amplify across the intact 15 kb in a standard PCR, so in WT only primer pairs that use D (inside the deleted region) give products: a larger FW–D band (~1000 bp) and a smaller FD–D band (~500 bp). In the homozygous deletion the D site is gone, so neither of those bands can form. Instead, closing the 15 kb gap brings R within range of the upstream primers, giving the deletion-junction band (~750 bp) only. The heterozygote carries both alleles and shows the sum: 1000 + 750 + 500. Only Profile 2 fits.",
    {"1": "The del lane cannot show a D-dependent 500 bp band; primer D's site is deleted.", "3": "The del lane cannot contain the ~1000 bp FW–D product, and WT shows an extra band.", "4": "The del lane shows a ~500 bp band, which requires primer D."})),
